## Workflow
- Every change of behaviour goes through `/task`; it proposes FULL, LIGHT or TRIVIAL and the user confirms. <!-- if:full -->
- FULL: planner → **G1** user approves the spec → tester RED → **G2** user approves the tests → commit <!-- if:full -->
  `task-NNN: RED tests approved` → developer → tester VERIFY → debugger (≤ 2 rounds, ≤ 5 attempts each) → <!-- if:full -->
  reviewer → doc-keeper → **G3** user verifies → commit `task-NNN: done`. <!-- if:full -->
- LIGHT: the main thread writes a mini-spec; one gate for spec and tests; reviewer and doc-keeper only when needed. <!-- if:full -->
- TRIVIAL (copy, typo, docs only, a config value): the main thread edits directly and the user confirms. <!-- if:full -->
- During `/task` the main thread writes only inside the task folder. Subagents get exact paths, and never a `name`. <!-- if:full -->
- Every subagent leaves one report in the task folder: line 1 `Verdict: <TOKEN>`, at most 300 lines. Its final <!-- if:full -->
  reply is `<VERDICT> <path>`. <!-- if:full -->
- Commits are local checkpoints, each after the user's approval. Never push: that is the user's job. <!-- if:full -->
- One task at a time until the loop is routine (`/task` › Parallel work). <!-- if:full -->
- Start every change in plan mode (Shift+Tab): goal, done when, out of scope, how to check. Build only after the user approves the plan. <!-- if:lite -->
- For anything bigger than a quick fix, save the approved plan as `tasks/NNN-slug/spec.md`. <!-- if:lite -->
  Copy it from `tasks/SPEC-TEMPLATE.md`. <!-- if:lite --> <!-- if:skills -->
- Failing tests first ("use red/green TDD"): write the tests, run them and show they fail for the right reason, then write the smallest code that makes them pass. <!-- if:lite -->
- One small task at a time. Before you report, run the full suite and compare the set of failing test IDs with the last run (the first baseline is in `tasks/000-setup/setup.md`). <!-- if:lite -->
- The user verifies each change before it is committed. Commits are local checkpoints, each after the user's approval. Never push: that is the user's job. <!-- if:lite -->
