## Guardrails (`.claude/hooks/guard.py`, settings in `.claude/hooks/guard.config.json`) <!-- if:guard -->
- **Blocks** (`guard.py`): subagent writes to protected paths or outside the subagent's role paths (other subagents are read-only); edits to committed tests by any subagent but the tester; files growing past their size limit. <!-- if:guard --> <!-- if:full -->
- **Blocks** (`guard.py`): subagent writes to protected paths and to committed tests; files growing past their size limit. <!-- if:guard --> <!-- if:lite -->
- **Asks the user** (`guard.py`): main-thread edits to committed tests and to protected paths (the setup files and the files the user owns, above). In bypass mode `guard.py` turns these asks into denials. <!-- if:guard -->
- **At the end of a turn** (`guard.py`): a subagent that grew an oversized file or changed a committed test it may not edit, even through the shell, is sent back once; the main thread gets a message instead. <!-- if:guard -->
- When `guard.py` blocks, follow its message; never retry the same thing through the shell. If `guard.py` itself errors, stop and tell the user: it fails closed, and can be switched off in `/hooks` if it is broken. <!-- if:guard -->

